#######################
# DISCARDED DCPS reconstructions 鈥?must not be published
#######################
# Written from a template in an earlier session on the wrong assumption that the
# original HotpotQA/PUPA DCPS scripts were lost. The real scripts were recovered
# from the dcps-artifact archive and faithfully ported to:
#   examples/papillon/dynamic_fewshot_nobase_subset.py
#   examples/hotpotqa/dynamic_fewshot_hotpotQA.py
#   examples/hotpotqa/dynamic_fewshot_hotpotQA_qwen.py
# The files below encode the wrong stage count (3 vs 4), the wrong metric,
# Top-K-then-test-all selection, a head-slice valset, and a retracted claim that
# the PUPA judge/untrusted LLM are fixed to gpt-4.1-mini. Delete them once a shell
# is available; ignored here so they cannot be committed by accident.
# NOTE: ignore rules do not untrack already-committed files 鈥?verify with
#   git ls-files examples/pupa examples/hotpotqa
examples/pupa/
examples/hotpotqa/dcps_search.py
examples/hotpotqa/dynamic_fewshot.py
examples/hotpotqa/dynamic_fewshot_gpt41mini.py

#######################
# Re-included by publish/assemble.* 鈥?NOT upstream
#######################
# `*.log` above also matches the paper's own run logs, which ship as
# provenance for the HoVer-extended and LiveBench runs. Keep the general
# rule (a user running an entrypoint should not commit its stdout) and
# carve out just these.
!examples/**/.run_*.log

# `*.jsonl` (line 232, added under a stray "# 鍦?.gitignore 鏂囦欢涓坊鍔?" comment)
# hides two sets of files that are the artifact rather than scratch output:
#
#   dcps_supplement/**/metric_logs/test.jsonl  - the four DCPS summary records.
#     Their test_score_pct values ARE the paper's Table 2(b) cells: LiveBench
#     65.08 / 59.52 and HoVer 56.67 / 54.67. The two LiveBench ones are the
#     cells the root README states are absent from clean_paper_data.csv, so
#     these files are that documented gap's only in-repo provenance.
#   examples/**/.checkpoints/*.jsonl  - the per-iteration search trajectory of
#     the same 228-iter HoVer and 60-iter LiveBench runs whose .run_*.log ship
#     above: one record per iteration carrying prompt, val_score,
#     fewshot_examples and usage_by_phase{tokens, cost_usd}. That token and
#     cost accounting is the first-hand source of the paper's T_M and Cost
#     columns, and the val_score series is the DCPS search itself.
#
# Anchored negations, NOT a blanket `!*.jsonl`: that would also re-include the
# AppleDouble ._wiki.abstracts.2017.jsonl and any future scratch .jsonl.
!dcps_supplement/experiment_runs/**/metric_logs/*.jsonl
!examples/**/.checkpoints/*.jsonl
